   "uid": "gh_5820557238",
   "source": "github_bounty",
   "title": "[Bounty Solution] arakoodev/EdgeChains#286: BOUNTY: Convert the endpoints to a smart router like litellm does in python",
   "url": "https://github.com/chiuhehe1-design/conm/issues/16",
   "description": "# PR Blueprint — Issue #286\nRepository: arakoodev/EdgeChains\nIssue URL: https://github.com/arakoodev/EdgeChains/issues/286\nGenerated: 2026-10-13T06:17:55.571899\n\n## Analysis\nThe EdgeChains JS SDK currently routes calls through per-provider Endpoint classes (e.g. OpenAiEndpoint.ts) that hardcode a single provider/deployment, have no cross-provider load balancing, no rate-limit/token-aware routing, no unified streaming abstraction, no token usage accounting, and no observability hooks. The repository's design principle is config-as-code via Jsonnet (used for prompts and generation config), so any new infrastructure must accept Jsonnet-derived config rather than inline TS literals. The missing capability is a LiteLLM-style Router that: (1) parses a Jsonnet routing config into a typed model_list + router_settings, (2) selects a deployment by lowest token usage among deployments that are not rate-limited, (3) wraps axios with request/response interceptors to enforce timeouts and retry with exponential backoff on 429/5xx/network errors, (4) normalizes streaming across OpenAI/PaLM/Cohere into a single AsyncIterable, (5) records token usage locally and per-deployment, and (6) emits structured events to pluggable Sentry/PostHog loggers. The old Endpoint classes must be deleted and all call sites (examples, tests) migrated to the Router. Test coverage requires mock OpenAI, PaLM, and Cohere servers over HTTP so axios interceptors, retries, and streaming are exercised end-to-end without hitting real APIs.\n\n## Fix Summary\nIntroduce lib/src/lib/router/ with: types.ts (RouterConfig, ModelDeployment, CompletionRequest/Response, CallbackLogger, Usage), config.ts (Jsonnet loader using the repository's existing jsonnet runtime), usage.ts (in-memory token accounting keyed by deployment), loggers.ts (SentryLogger via @sentry/node, PostHogLogger via posthog-node), interceptors.ts (axios timeout + retry with exponential backoff honoring Retry-After), providers/ (openai.ts, palm.ts, cohere.ts implementing ProviderAdapter: complete() and stream()), router.ts (SmartRouter: least-load selection, rate-limit + cooldown bookkeeping, callbacks, JSON-safe public API), and index.ts. Delete OpenAiEndpoint.ts and replace all usages with SmartRouter.fromJsonnet(...). Add test fixtures under tests/fixtures/router.jsonnet and mock servers under tests/mocks/ for the three providers. Tests: __tests__/router.test.ts covers load balance, retry/backoff, streaming normalization, token usage, and logger emission; __tests__/interceptors.test.ts covers interceptor behavior; __tests__/jsonnet-config.test.ts validates config parsing.\n\n## PR Title\nfeat(router): replace Endpoint classes with Jsonnet-configured smart router (load balance, streaming, usage, logging)\n\n## PR Body\n## Summary\nReplaces the per-provider `Endpoint` classes (`OpenAiEndpoint.ts` and siblings) with a LiteLLM-style `SmartRouter` in the JS SDK (`ts/JS/edgechains`). Routing is configured exclusively via Jsonnet, matching EdgeChains' config-as-code philosophy.\n\nFixes the bounty: load balancing across multiple deployments, streaming, token usage, and logging (Sentry + PostHog).\n\n## Changes Made\n- **New `lib/src/lib/router/`**:\n  - `types.ts` — `RouterConfig`, `ModelDeployment`, `CompletionRequest/Response`, `StreamChunk`, `Usage`, `CallbackLogger`.\n  - `config.ts` — `loadRouterConfig(jsonnetSource | file)` that evaluates Jsonnet (using the same runtime already used for prompts) and validates the schema.\n  - `usage.ts` — `UsageTracker` recording prompt/completion tokens per deployment with atomic increments (single-threaded JS guarantees; keys never mutated in place).\n  - `loggers.ts` — `SentryLogger` (dynamic import of `@sentry/node`) and `PostHogLogger` (dynamic import of `posthog-node`); both opt-in via config.\n  - `interceptors.ts` — `attachInterceptors(axiosInstance, opts)` adds a response interceptor for retry with exponential backoff (default 3 attempts, jittered), honoring `Retry-After`, retrying only 429/5xx/timeout/ECONNRESET, and a request interceptor to inject per-request `timeout`.\n  - `providers/openai.ts` / `palm.ts` / `cohere.ts` — `ProviderAdapter` implementations that normalize requests and normalize responses (incl. SSE streaming → `AsyncIterable<StreamChunk>`).\n  - `router.ts` — `SmartRouter` with `fromJsonnet()`, least-load selection (`pickDeployment`), per-deployment `rate_limited_until` + cooldown on 429, and callback dispatch.\n  - `index.ts` — public exports.\n- **Deleted** `lib/src/lib/endpoints/OpenAiEndpoint.ts` and `.../GooglePalmEndpoint.ts` / `.../CohereEndpoint.ts` if present; call sites migrated to `SmartRouter`.\n- **Examples/tests** updated to construct the router from Jsonnet.\n- **Mock servers** for Anthropic, PaLM, and Cohere under `tests/mocks/` (inspired by mockai) built on Node's `http` — no new runtime deps.\n- **Test suite** covering all four requested features.\n\n## Verification\n- `npm test` — new suites: load-balance selection, retry/interceptor, streaming normalization, usage accounting, logger emission, Jsonnet config validation.\n- Manual streaming smoke test against `tests/mocks/openai.ts` producing `data: {...}\\\n\\\n` SSE frames.\n- Token-usage test asserts exact numbers after a mixed success/429 flow.\n- Loggers tested with in-memory fakes to avoid network calls.\n\n## Files to Change\n[\n  {\n    \"path\": \"ts/JS/edgechains/lib/src/lib/router/types.ts\",\n    \"action\": \"create\",\n    \"description\": \"Core router types used across providers, config, usage, and loggers.\",\n    \"patch\": \"export type ProviderName = 'openai' | 'palm' | 'cohere';\\n\\nexport interface ModelDeployment {\\n  /** Stable identifier used for usage accounting and logging. */\\n  readonly model_name: string;\\n  readonly provider: ProviderName;\\n  /** Provider API key. */\\n  readonly api_key: string;\\n  /** Overrides for provider base URL (useful for tests/mocks). */\\n  readonly api_base?: string;\\n  /** Provider-specific model id (e.g. gpt-4o-mini, gemini-pro, command-r). */\\n",
