ons: triage failures the same day and fix flaky tests at the root cause, including ones caused by unreliable third-party sandboxes Run release-day regression and the OWASP ZAP security scan, and give a clear go / no-go call Migrate the remaining legacy tests and decide what’s worth automating and what stays manual Coach developers so they own their tests, and organise QA days with the other product teams What we are looking for 5+ years in QA on web applications Hands-on experience testing REST APIs and integrations with external systems (Postman, Playwright API testing or similar), including authentication flows like OAuth and webhooks At least 2 years writing and maintaining test automation in code (Playwright, Cypress or Selenium, ideally TypeScript/JavaScript), not only record-and-play tools Strong exploratory testing skills, with bug reports developers can act on without follow-up questions You’ve defined a test strategy (what to automate, what to test manually, coverage), not only executed test cases Experience running automated tests in CI (GitHub Actions or similar) You get developers to adopt new habits through pairing, good examples and clear specs, not by policing Nice to haves Experience with complex B2B SaaS, ideally with a public API or integration marketplace Contract testing (e.g. Pact) or mocking third-party services Playwright specifically, and Gherkin / BDD Experience leading a shift-left change Testing integrations with accounting or finance software Basic security testing (e.g. OWASP ZAP) What you’ll get Competitive salary based on experience, plus 8% holiday allowance A results-based bonus based on company performance (up to a full 13th month's salary) 25 vacation days to recharge Earn an extra day of PTO for each year at Rentman, from your second anniversary up to five years. A 4-week paid sabbatical after 5 years to go on an adventure Flexible WFH policy & work from anywhere for 4 weeks a year Pension plan through BrightPensioen An annual training budget to gro",
