   "url": "https://github.com/603-Identity/devcontainers/issues/26",
   "description": "> **Re-planned 2026-11-02 under the [#418 design](https://github.com/603-Identity/devcontainers/issues/418#issuecomment-6584294809).** The shared template is now dev-App only, and the PAT route is frozen (decision 1). **glunk-works** rows adopt the dev-App flavour once #418's milestone ships v1.6. **603-Identity** rows wait for 603-Identity's own dev-App cutover.\n>\n> A dev-App adoption:\n> - copies `template/.devcontainer/` and sets only the four per-repo surfaces: the token mount `tokens/<owner>/<repo>`; `FROM` `devcontainer-devapp` or `devcontainer-devapp-tofu`; the root-run Dockerfile extras; an optional loopback `appPort`;\n> - copies only `devcontainer-image.yml` and `secret-scan.yml` from `template/.github/workflows/`;\n> - runs the way-of-working plugin's review gate;\n> - has its approval ruleset (at least 1 approval, code-owner review) live before the dev App is installed.\n>\n> Lines the re-plan changed are marked *(re-planned)*.\n\n## Scope\n\nAdopt the template on every Python repo, moving each to the image's standard: **Python 3.14 system interpreter, uv-native project layout** (`pyproject.toml` with `[dependency-groups]`, committed `uv.lock`, `uv sync --locked`, `uv run`). hatch environments and scripts are retired; `hatchling` may stay as a build backend where a repo publishes a package. Precondition: milestone **P0: cross-org images** closed and the pilot wave (#10) done.\n\n| Repo | Today | Change at adoption |\n|---|---|---|\n| glunk-works/bounty-infra | CI 3.11 lint/test, 3.14 package; hatch envs `lint`, `test`, `audit`, `sbom` in `src/pyproject.toml`; `python` Feature | CI to 3.14; hatch envs become dependency groups, scripts become `uv run` lines; `uv.lock` committed; drop the Feature and lockfile |\n| glunk-works/pm-agent-loop | CI 3.12; hatch envs `default`, `types` | same migration; CI to 3.14 |\n| glunk-works/scope-core | CI 3.11 + 3.14; hatch envs `lint`, `test` | same migration; CI to 3.14 |\n| 603-Identity/tenant-posture-assessment | CI 3.12; `requirements.in` + `requirements.txt` | *(re-planned: deferred to 603-Identity's dev-App cutover)* `pyproject.toml` + `uv.lock` replace both files; CI to 3.14 (supersedes the framing of #11); bc-detect-secrets 1.5.51 baseline regenerated |\n\nPer-repo adoption PR checklist:\n- [ ] *(re-planned)* copy `template/.devcontainer/` and set only the four per-repo surfaces (see the note at the top); `FROM` `devcontainer-devapp` by tag@digest; the `-venv` volume is part of the shared template\n- [ ] add `.devcontainer` to `dependabot.yml` (docker ecosystem) and switch the Python entry to `package-ecosystem: uv`\n- [ ] `pyproject.toml`: `[project]` with `requires-python = \">=3.14\"`, `[dependency-groups]` for dev/lint/test (and `checkov` where a local gate uses it, pinned to the ledger version); `uv lock`; commit `uv.lock`\n- [ ] `.python-version` only if the repo must stay below 3.14 during migration; otherwise omit\n- [ ] CI: pinned `astral-sh/setup-uv`, `uv sync --locked`, `uv run <tool>`; `python-version` pins to 3.14; `pip install hatch` removed\n- [ ] *(re-planned)* no per-repo `postCreateCommand`: the shared template runs `pre-commit install` only, and `uv sync --locked` (plus `--group checkov` where used) runs from the repo's own gate\n- [ ] `.ai/project.yml` `gates.green` and CLAUDE.md commands rewritten from `hatch run ...` to `uv run ...`\n- [ ] delete the repo's old `.devcontainer/Dockerfile`, Features and `devcontainer-lock.json`\n- [ ] *(re-planned)* approval ruleset live first; the plugin's review gate; `devcontainer-image.yml` and `secret-scan.yml` copied from the template\n- [ ] gate green inside the container; CI green with the new pins\n- [ ] old container and `vsc-*` image removed on the host\n\nNot in this wave: loop-orchestrator (documented exception, see the threat-model issue). When it is migrated later, it follows the same uv-native layout.\n\n",
