   "title": "Time Field Atlas 1.4.3 on a phone with 8 GB of memory",
   "url": "https://github.com/0x94t3z/fieldatlas/issues/2",
   "description": "## The task\n\nOnly a 6 GB Redmi 13C has been timed properly so far. Time Field Atlas on a phone with **8 GB** of memory (an arm64 phone with Android 13 or later).\n\nInstall [Field Atlas 1.4.3](https://github.com/0x94t3z/fieldatlas/releases/tag/v1.4.3), download **Qwen3.5 4B** in setup (setup recommends it there), add the **Encyclopedia** and **Essentials** collections (the questions use their passages and places; together about 12 GB to download and 27 GB of free storage), turn on airplane mode, ask the 10 questions in [the timing template](https://github.com/0x94t3z/fieldatlas/blob/main/docs/fieldtest/device-timings/TEMPLATE.md), and write down the time each finished answer shows.\n\n## Accepted when\n\n- A pull request adds `docs/fieldtest/device-timings/<phone-model>.md`, copied from the template, with every question either timed or marked *stopped* or *error* in the Finished? column.\n- It uploads to the pull request on GitHub the three screenshots, the photo and the screen recording the template asks for, with the code word from the assignment comment; the memory screenshot shows physical RAM of 8 GB, and More shows 1.4.3. Links to images hosted elsewhere are not accepted. Black out the phone number, serial number and IMEI if the screen shows them; never post or send them.\n- The phone is a real phone, not an emulator ([CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/0x94t3z/fieldatlas/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#contributor-rewards), \"A real phone, shown\").\n- The phone model is not already listed in `docs/fieldtest/device-timings/`.\n\n## How to take it\n\nComment \"taking this\" and wait to be assigned; only the assigned person is paid. If there is no pull request within 7 days, the maintainer unassigns it and the task opens up again. Put `Closes #<this issue>` and `Base address: 0x…` in the pull request description as plain lines (the template has a place for them). Rules: [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/0x94t3z/fieldatlas/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#contributor-rewards).\n\nReward: 5,000,000 ATLAS\n",
