ate a competitive advantage, or expose the company to being left behind Turn watch findings into actionable inputs for the R&D/Innovation roadmap and for COMEX-level strategic discussions Build and maintain a structured watch process (sources, cadence, internal distribution) rather than ad hoc monitoring Capability audit Regularly map and assess the company's technical capabilities (skills, tools, infrastructure, external dependencies) Identify areas of risk, over-investment, under-investment, or critical dependency Benchmark our capabilities against the market and competitors Technology strategy Contribute to defining the company's technology strategy alongside the Strategy & Operations Director Assess build, buy, partner, or acquisition opportunities on technology topics Inform R&D resource allocation decisions with a strategic and financial lens Reporting and governance Produce syntheses and recommendations for COMEX on tech-strategy topics Set up tracking indicators on technical execution vs. commitments made Participate in R&D/Innovation committees as an independent strategic voice Candidate profile Experience 5-6 years of overall experience, engineering background (degree in engineering or equivalent) Ideal trajectory: 2-3 years of hands-on technical execution, followed by 2-3 years in a hybrid technical/business role e.g. Engineer → Technical Product Manager, Engineer → tech-focused strategy consulting, or Engineer → Chief of Staff to a CTO/VP Engineering Profiles with only pure execution experience (no exposure to business trade-offs) or only early technical experience followed by years of generalist consulting (no longer technically credible) are not a fit for this role Given the seniority level, the candidate should compensate for limited years of experience with either deep, recognized expertise in a specific technical domain (enough to be seen as a peer by R&D on that topic) or a strong, proven track record of challenging senior stakeholders from a strategy/consulting back",
