ectly, you’ll also become a true expert in our product. What will you be doing? Running your own outbound motion through cold calls, emails and LinkedIn to build pipeline from the ground up, working closely with our high-performing BDRs Owning the full sales cycle from first call to closed-won, typically within a short sales cycle Qualifying SMB prospects across multiple industries Running discovery that uncovers real pain and moves deals forward Delivering demos tailored to each buyer, including technical stakeholders Hitting and exceeding monthly and quarterly targets for pipeline generation, activities and closed revenue Keeping HubSpot up to date for accurate forecasting What are we looking for? At least 2 to 3 years in a closing role running a full outbound sales cycle with a track record of closing high-volume SMB deals A strong outbound background, ideally as a BDR or SDR - you’re comfortable picking up the phone 50+ times a day and know how to hook a prospect in the first 30 seconds SaaS sales experience is a must - you know what an API is and can hold your own in a conversation with a technical buyer Consistent quota attainment and overachievement A hunter mindset and the ownership to build your own pipeline and drive your own metrics Sharp, instinctive discovery skills - you can uncover pain efficiently Curiosity and the drive to become a product expert, so every conversation is relevant and consultative Fluency in English and French Familiarity with HubSpot is a nice to have Genuine excitement for what Prelude is building What do we offer? Competitive base salary with uncapped commission + BSPCEs Hybrid working style: 4 days in-office in Paris, 1 day remote High-end gear and ergonomic setup 100% travel subsidised to our Paris office Private health insurance Swile meal vouchers Gym pass Annual offsites in great locations The opportunity to be part of building something big, from the start! Interview process Meet a member of the Talent team Interview with H