   "url": "https://github.com/XHToken/Spark-X2.6/issues/16",
   "description": "# HER Hack-Astron # 7 | Spark-X2.6 Open Source AI for Good Challenge\r\n\r\nBuild something useful for people who need it. This round invites you to use **Spark-X2.6-4B** to create a working application for disaster response, health, accessibility, gender equality, or another public-interest need.\r\n\r\n**Go to [Spark-X2.6-4B on Hugging Face](https://huggingface.co/XHToken/Spark-X2.6-4B), give the model a ❤️ Like, and download and use it to build your application. Publish your complete project with a video or illustrated demo in the model's Hugging Face Community Discussions, then reply to this event Issue with the Discussion link.**\r\n\r\n- Model and getting started: https://huggingface.co/XHToken/Spark-X2.6-4B\r\n- Publish your project (Hugging Face Community Discussions): https://huggingface.co/XHToken/Spark-X2.6-4B/discussions\r\n- Submit your Discussion link (reply to this event Issue): https://github.com/XHToken/Spark-X2.6/issues/16\r\n\r\n## Quick Summary\r\n\r\n1. Individuals of any gender are welcome. For team entries, at least 50% of contributors must identify as women, following the HER Hack-Astron participation rule.\r\n2. Your application must actually use Spark-X2.6-4B. Explain what the model does in the application.\r\n3. Every submission must include **a video demo OR an illustrated demo with screenshots and explanatory text** showing the application running.\r\n4. Publish the complete entry in Spark-X2.6-4B's Hugging Face Community Discussions, then reply to this announcement Issue with the direct Discussion link.\r\n5. AI-assisted development is allowed; disclose how it was used. AI personas must not be presented as human participants.\r\n6. No live presentation is required.\r\n7. One winner receives **USD 100**. No upfront participation or prize-claim fee is required.\r\n\r\n## Schedule\r\n\r\n- Submissions open: **October 23, 2026 (UTC)**\r\n- Submission deadline: **October 31, 2026, 23:59 UTC**\r\n- Beijing time equivalent of the deadline: **November 1, 2026, 07:59 (UTC+8)**\r\n- Judging and winner announcement: after submissions close; updates will be posted in this Issue.\r\n\r\n**UTC is the authoritative time zone for the event.**\r\n\r\n## Challenge Tracks\r\n\r\nChoose one or combine several. Other applications with a clear public benefit are also welcome.\r\n\r\n- **Disaster preparedness and response**: organize public emergency information, structure requests for assistance, match supply information, or support multilingual communication.\r\n- **Health and well-being**: explain health education materials in plain language, support appointment preparation, or help users keep health and care records.\r\n- **Accessibility**: simplify complex text, assist with reading and communication, or help people navigate public services.\r\n- **Gender equality**: identify and explain gender bias in text, improve access to support resources, or create tools supporting equal participation in education and employment.\r\n- **Other public-interest applications**: elder support, inclusive education, environmental protection, community mutual aid, or volunteer coordination.\r\n\r\nFocus on a specific group of users and a concrete problem. Show how your application helps them and where its limitations remain.\r\n\r\n## How to Participate\r\n\r\n1. Visit [Spark-X2.6-4B on Hugging Face](https://huggingface.co/XHToken/Spark-X2.6-4B), click **❤️ Like**, and follow the model card to download and run the model.\r\n2. Build a working application that uses Spark-X2.6-4B. Record the model revision, runtime, hardware, precision or quantization, and key inference settings. If using a mirror, identify the source and corresponding revision.\r\n3. Prepare **one of the following required demo formats**:\r\n   - **Video demo**: a screen recording showing the scenario, user input, application workflow, and actual output. A duration of 2–5 minutes is recommended.\r\n   - **Illustrated demo**: screenshots with step-by-step explanations showing the same end-to-end workflow. Include actual inputs and outputs.\r\n   \r\n   Concept slides, promotional images, or descriptions without a running demonstration are insufficient.\r\n4. Create a **new Discussion in [Spark-X2.6-4B's Hugging Face Community](https://huggingface.co/XHToken/Spark-X2.6-4B/discussions)**. Include `HER Hack-Astron # 7` in the title, for example: `[HER Hack-Astron # 7] [Open Source AI for Good] <Project name>`.\r\n\r\n   Publish the complete project description, video or illustrated demo, model usage, and reproduction instructions in that Discussion. Embed screenshots or provide publicly accessible video links, and check that reviewers can access them.\r\n5. Reply to **[this event's GitHub Issue](https://github.com/XHToken/Spark-X2.6/issues/16)** with the direct Discussion link, for example: `https://huggingface.co/XHToken/Spark-X2.6-4B/discussions/<number>`. This completes your submission. For team entries, also list all contributors and their profiles in your reply. Keep subsequent project updates in the same Discussion.\r\n\r\n**Submission requires both steps: publish the complete project in the designated Hugging Face Community Discussion, then leave its link in this event's GitHub Issue. GitHub-only or other-platform-only submissions are not accepted.**\r\n\r\n## Submission Template\r\n\r\nCopy the following into your Hugging Face Discussion:\r\n\r\n```markdown\r\n## Project name and track\r\nProject name:\r\nTrack:\r\n\r\n## Who this helps and what problem it solves\r\nTarget users:\r\nConcrete scenario and problem:\r\nExpected public benefit:\r\n\r\n## How Spark-X2.6-4B is used\r\nModel source and revision:\r\nThe model's role in the application:\r\nOther models, tools, or services used, if any:\r\n\r\n## Demo (required: video OR illustrated walkthrough)\r\nVideo link / embedded screenshots:\r\nExample input:\r\nApplication workflow and actual output:\r\n\r\n## How to reproduce\r\nCode repository or runnable example, if available:\r\nSetup and run instructions:\r\nRuntime and versions:\r\nHardware and precision/quantization:\r\nKey prompts and inference settings:\r\n\r\n## Results and limitations\r\nOb",
