   "url": "https://github.com/Saiaaax/CyberNinja-Dojo/issues/2",
   "description": "**Bounty:** $10 (LT)\n\n**Area:** build.py diagnostic artifact management\n\n**Current state:** The `--retention-report` flag reports stale artifacts but does not provide a CI-friendly exit code. CI pipelines need a way to fail when stale artifacts exceed a threshold, preventing accidental inclusion of outdated diagnostics in PRs.\n\n**What is needed:** Add a `--check-stale` flag that exits non-zero when older diagnostic artifacts exist, suitable for use as a CI gate.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:**\n- Add `--check-stale` flag to `build.py` that exits 1 if any older (non-current-commit) artifacts exist, exits 0 otherwise\n- Add `--max-stale-bytes` option (default: 0 = any stale is an error) to allow a byte threshold\n- The flag is read-only and does not delete artifacts\n- Add at least 4 tests with a temporary diagnostic directory\n- Document the flag in `docs/OPERATIONS.md`\n- Include the diagnostic build artifacts from `python3 build.py`\n\nCommissions:\n\nYou can earn an extra $5 for every bounty issue you create on your own fork of the repo, provided you keep up with submissions. We will payout the bounty you place between $5 and $25 to the submitter and you will earn an extra $5 on your payout, after you merge the best submission for your bounty. You are required to use this exact issue template & description format, including this message and the required validation. Payouts will not be given to you or other submitters without a valid issue or you registered the following details. You are required to rename your fork to something fun and unique, and provide this exact message in your issue description. The required validation includes running `python3 build.py`, including the generated diagnostic `.logd` artifact, and using the PR template.\n\nRequired validation:\n- Run `python3 build.py`\n- Include the generated diagnostic `.logd` artifact from `diagnostic/build-XXX.logd` in the PR notes; this must be a real diagnostic log and must not be `diagnostic/build-00000000.logd`\n- Include the matching diagnostic JSON metadata if present\n- You must use `.github/pull_request_template.md` for your submission",
