rm, while you'll define, oversee, and continuously improve the security measures that protect it. We're already SOC 2 compliant, with ISO 27001 and additional certifications on the horizon. Operating across multiple regions and working with 20+ data providers also brings interesting challenges around data privacy, vendor security, and international regulations. This is a hands-on role with significant autonomy, direct exposure to leadership, and the opportunity to build a security function that grows alongside the business. What You'll Do: Security & Infrastructure Own and continuously improve our application and infrastructure security posture, partnering with Engineering to implement and maintain effective security controls. Lead our vulnerability management program, including external penetration testing, vulnerability disclosure, and remediation tracking. Identify, assess, and prioritize security risks, ensuring vulnerabilities are addressed based on their potential business impact. Compliance & Certifications Own our security compliance program end to end, maintaining SOC 2 and leading future certifications such as ISO 27001. Manage ongoing evidence collection, auditor relationships, control assessments, and remediation activities. Develop and maintain a scalable compliance roadmap aligned with business growth and customer requirements. Security Governance & Risk Management Develop and maintain security policies, risk assessments, and our company-wide risk register. Lead regular access reviews, security awareness initiatives, and incident response preparedness. Coordinate security incidents and drive continuous improvements to our security processes and controls. Corporate IT & Identity Management Own our corporate IT security framework, including device management (MDM), identity providers, SSO, and SaaS access controls. Oversee secure employee onboarding and offboarding, account provisioning, and hardware inventory management, working with our operational IT team on execution. ",
