   "title": "Tell HN: Getting spam after commenting on monthly Who's Hiring posts. Who else?",
   "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50153608",
   "description": "I made a post on the monthly Who&#x27;s Hiring thread, and since then I&#x27;ve been inundated by spammy AI slop messages of people pitching their vibe coded job search platforms. It&#x27;s junk mail to the point that I probably won&#x27;t post on a Who&#x27;s Hiring thread again. I&#x27;m looking for real opportunities, not to sign up for yet another person&#x27;s dead end job search platform. I&#x27;m just curious if other HN folks have had the same experience recently? Here&#x27;s the email I just got today: &gt; I&#x27;m Kelvin — I run Loker Dollar, a small job board for remote roles that pay in USD. I came across your post on Hacker News&#x27;s “Who wants to be hired?” thread — the React Native, React + JavaScript one, based in Nomadic. US and EU, and it&#x27;s exactly the kind of profile the companies we work with are hiring for. &gt; Being upfront about what I did: I added an anonymized version of your post to our recruiter search so hiring teams can find you. Your name and email stay hidden — nobody sees them unless you say yes. &gt; Two one-click choices, no account needed: &gt; Claim & manage my profile &gt; Decide how you appear and who can reach you. &gt; Remove me &gt; Delete the listing, and I&#x27;ll never email you again. I&#x27;m not sure what, if anything, can be done to prevent people scraping and spamming these threads, but I do feel that these threads are being abused, and I really wish there were a way to only allow people who have verified opportunities to contact me about their own opportunities.",
