   "source": "hn",
   "title": "Tell HN: Don't mass spam employers with LLM generated emails",
   "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50095323",
   "description": "If you&#x27;re looking for a job, do -not- have Claude bulk email every company on &quot;Who&#x27;s Hiring&quot;. These things all look the same and your message is just going to get marked spam. For example, it&#x27;s painfully obvious that our staff eng role&#x27;s &quot;combination of distributed execution, workload optimization, and cost-aware infrastructure&quot; is not, in fact, &quot;unusually close&quot; to whatever line on your resume Claude decided is tangentially relevant. Just write a normal email by hand and send it. If you it looks like you spent 5 minutes looking up what we do and are actually excited I&#x27;ll at least look at your resume; if you spent 0 minutes thinking about the job posting I&#x27;m going to spend 0 minutes on this too.",
