   "source": "github_bounty",
   "title": "[MAJOR] Analyse VEGR term weighting and report coverage weakness up front",
   "url": "https://github.com/emrsyah/needle/issues/15",
   "description": "**Severity:** major · **Raised by reviewer(s):** B, C\r\n\r\n**Location:** `src/needle/rewards/__init__.py:23-29, 182-194`; abstract; Table 4.1\r\n\r\n### Problem\r\nEvidence and retrieval terms supply up to 3 of VEGR's ~5 points. A wrong answer citing gold sentences can score high: the first R0 s7 episode has EM 0 and a VEGR total of 2.87. VEGR coverage (0.473 / 0.513 / 0.333) is *below* untrained B0 (0.472) on 2 of 3 seeds, but the abstract only highlights precision of 0.73–0.75.\r\n\r\n### Why it matters\r\nThis is selective reporting, and the weighting may explain why EM doesn't move between R0 and R1.\r\n\r\n### Suggested fix\r\n- From existing rollouts, report each term's share of within-group reward variance and the fraction of high-reward rollouts with EM = 0 (CPU).\r\n- State in the abstract that VEGR does not raise coverage, and pair this with the R3 trade-off.\r\n\r\n---\r\n_From the simulated IEEE peer review of the thesis (3 independent reviewers, merged). Tracked in the summary issue._",
   "budget_min": null,
   "budget_max": null,
   "currency": "USD",
