cy Directive Anticipate compensation risks and pay equity gaps before they surface, and put guardrails in place to prevent them Model costs and impact for new or changing programs, using AI and advanced analytics in modeling, benchmarking, and program design, and set how the team applies those tools Deliver data-driven compensation guidance to executives, business leaders, and HR colleagues across every region and function Partner with HR Technology to maintain job architecture and compensation programs in Workday and adjacent systems Lead our participation in compensation surveys, analyzing results to assess competitiveness and meet pay equity reporting requirements Make compensation concepts land — build creative, non-traditional enablement for TAPs, HRBPs, managers, and employees in formats people actually use, not just slide decks and webinars Manage, mentor, and develop a lean global team of compensation professionals Lead compensation workstreams during mergers and acquisitions What you’ll bring 10+ years leading compensation programs in large global technology organizations, public and private, including people management Proven ability to design and implement compensation strategies for a globally dispersed workforce Exceptional analytical depth — you build the models, stress-test the assumptions, and turn the output into a defensible recommendation Working knowledge of AI in compensation — pay design for AI/ML and other scarce technical talent, plus hands-on use of AI tools for analytics, modeling, and reporting Command of the EU Pay Transparency Directive and comparable pay equity regimes — you lead job leveling, gap reporting, and multi-country transparency readiness, not just monitor it In-depth knowledge of leading global benchmark survey methodologies and practices Strong judgment and attention to detail on sensitive, confidential, time-critical matters Influential leadership and relationship-building skills across business and HR audiences at every level Strong project ",
