rd Assessments (FHA), Failure Mode Effect Analyses (FMEA) and System Safety Assessments (SSA), in accordance with applicable airworthiness and safety standards. Identify and assess applicable certification requirements, means of compliance and industry standards, including relevant aspects of EASA SC E-19, and ensure that certification considerations are addressed throughout the development cycle. Coordinate the electric engine development and qualification test campaigns, in collaboration with the testing team, including the definition of test plans, objectives, and success criteria. Review and assess test results, identify technical risks and deviations, and coordinate the resolution of issues encountered during testing. Prepare and review technical documentation, including specifications, interface documents, design reviews, qualification reports, and compliance statements. Support prototype build, aircraft integration and ground/flight testing activities throughout the maturation of the propulsion system Your Profile: Master’s degree or PhD in Electrical Engineering, Aerospace Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Mechatronics or a related technical field. At least 8 years of relevant professional experience in the development, integration or testing of electric motors, engine controllers/inverters or integrated electric-drive systems. Strong knowledge of electric machines and power electronics, including motor topologies, inverter architectures, operating characteristics & limits, losses & thermal behaviour, motor control strategies & protection functions, and manufacturing processes. Broad understanding of electric engine development, including thermal management, insulation systems, high-voltage systems, EMC, mechanical integrity, reliability & durability, and system integration. Experience defining and managing technical requirements, specifications, interfaces and verification strategies for electric engines or electric-drive systems. Experience collaborating with external dev",
