   "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50287623",
   "description": "I have been applying for jobs since this year, and I have been hanging in by the threads. For the past 7 years I have been doing freelance work, and it&#x27;s been great until the AI boom. I am a software developer with 13 years of experience, and this year is the first time I am getting frustrated with my career. I have no money to help myself or my family. I have this little space in my house that can help me start up a small chicken poultry farm, but I have no funds for it. All my savings exhausted. If I can raise 2k usd, that should be enough to get me started with 200 layer birds. I believe that this startup capital will keep me engaged and also help me provide for my family going forward. It&#x27;s looking like tech will no longer be the dream job as it used to be. I am sorry for bringing this here, The people around me cannot help give me the loan I need, and banks will not give it to me if there is no history of my activity doing farming. Any help or job will be appreciated. Thanks alot. Jeff",
