   "description": "About the company From lithium for electric vehicle batteries, to copper for wind turbines, and rare earth elements for electronics, critical minerals are the building blocks of our energy transition and our broader future. Exploration needs more discoveries than ever before. Lithosquare radically speeds up mineral exploration by combining foundational AI, geological expertise, and real-world data to reduce uncertainty, prioritize the right targets, reduce costs and accelerate discovery. Based in Paris, Lithosquare gathered an exceptional team of geologists, scientists, AI engineers, and data specialists to work as one, from field sampling to model optimization, and push the boundaries of what's possible. About the job As an Asset Strategist at Lithosquare, you are the catalyst bridging complex geoscience, foundational AI, and high-stakes executive decisions. You will own the end-to-end impact of our partners’ engagements, embedding with top mining operators to transform real-world geological data into high-value mining assets. You will operate directly at the intersection of technology, physical operations, and energy-transition strategy. Working alongside geologists, data scientists, and external leadership, you will serve as the primary driver for project velocity and value creation. What you'll do Reporting to the VP Asset Development, your main responsibilities will include: Drive partnership deployments: Own the overall operational execution of exploration partnerships, ensuring Lithosquare’s AI outputs and geology expertise translate directly into high-confidence target prioritization, accelerated field discovery and the development of valuable mining assets. Lead multi-disciplinary squads: Organize cross-functional internal teams of geologists, data scientists, and AI engineers to deliver exploration roadmaps aligned with critical partner milestones. Build strategic trust: Develop advisory-level relationships with partner executives and field operations teams, navigating complex organizations to identify strategic expansion opportunities. Accelerate the product loop: Feed operational challenges and geological edge-cases back to our core R&D teams to continuously evolve our AI platform. What we are looking for 5–7+ years of high-impact experience in top-tier strategy consulting, tech deployment strategy, or mining project development. Experience in mining exploration projects is a bonus, but not mandatory. Proven high autonomy & drive: A track record of steering complex, ambiguous projects to completion in fast-paced or field-intensive environments. Degree in Engineering, Geoscience, or Management , with an ability to comfortably converse and create trust with AI engineers, field geologists, and corporate executives alike. Commercial & product instincts: Strong ability to spot expansion opportunities, articulate ROI, and translate operational needs into product features. Mission alignment: Deeply motivated by solving physical-world engineering challenges to secure the critical minerals driving the energy transition. Global readiness: Fluency in English with experience managing international multi-stakeholder environments. Perks & Benefits 🏢 Offices located in the heart of Paris 🌱 Strong culture of ownership & entrepreneurship 🌍 Opportunity to significantly contribute to energy transition 👥 Collaborative work environment with world-class experts in geology, AI, and data science 🏋️ Gym pass 🎉 Frequent team drinks, events & regular off-sites 💰 Competitive salary package Join Lithosquare and become part of a passionate team driving innovation at the intersection of AI and Earth exploration. Let's make a tangible difference together! Find Jobs in France on Arbeitnow",
