   "title": "Show HN: Multipeer, a multiplayer infinite canvas for people and their agents",
   "url": "https://multipeer.sh",
   "description": "I&#x27;m building Multipeer, a desktop app for running agents, tools and working wth teammates on one shared canvas. I often have several agent sessions open at once, but they&#x27;re all scattered across terminals. It was also hard for my co-founder to see what my agents are doing or jump in to work together. So We built the solution to our own problem. And now we&#x27;re releasing it to the world. It&#x27;s a macOS app for now (soon on Windows and Linux). You can invite your teammates over a local network or over the internet. They can follow your view and, if you allow them, they can also take control of your terminal and claude code&#x2F;codex sessions. The app is still early, and I&#x27;m also releasing the iPhone&#x2F;Android app soon to remotely control everything on your canvas. I&#x27;d would like to get feedback from the HN community! If there&#x27;s any features you&#x27;d like to see, please contact me via: shyam@multipeer.sh, we build really fast. I&#x27;d love to talk to everyone of you and work on your feedback! Thanks!",
